## What actually passed

The same fresh VM audited and removed ten selected SDK children: 58,008 nodes
(53,276 leaves, 4,732 directories). The SDK root and unselected root-name set
were preserved. Free disk rose from 14,347,419,648 to 23,306,887,168 bytes,
above the unchanged 18,241,982,464-byte preacquisition threshold. The frozen
setup check and the separate live capacity gate passed before acquisition.

Only selected SDK nodes on the disposable VM were deleted. Recovery there
requires reinstall/replacement. The Mac SDK was not touched.

The accepted software acquisition made its four bounded HTTPS responses with
zero retries and matched the pinned ZIP/tar hashes. The unchanged native
harness and independent PID supervisor then passed. One generator guardian
and one importer guardian used nine generated files totaling 28,742 bytes.
Two software roots were extracted; no Docker container was started.

Both owned workspaces, two owned cgroups, the owned Docker container/image and
the newly acquired input were retired, with the applicable closed receipts
verified. This is normal owned cleanup under the trusted VM/provider premise,
not guardian-death or whole-job-teardown proof.

## Evidence checked and retained

The sole downloaded result ZIP was 4,697 bytes, artifact `10729773444`, SHA-256
`4a2709311ea4ce34298c0fe11ab6ad6c0feaf1c00a37b730ce349f8673b61be1`.
Its exact five canonical aggregates total 10,004 bytes. They are retained
privately under `artifacts/lumi-sft-prepared-qualification-v0.3/`.
The new prefix receipt is stored there too; the older prefix receipt at its
historical path is unchanged. No raw job logs or software archive were
downloaded to the Mac.

The authenticated v3 verifier was run read-only against these receipts, with
only its prefix-report data path remapped to this run. Its recomputed result
matches the uploaded verification byte-for-byte. An independent second audit
confirmed that result, all 22 plan bindings (exact approved activation exception)
and all 78 native source hashes. No native work was executed locally.

Before publication, 301 unique synthetic tests passed on each of Python 3.11.15
and 3.13.7; an independent fresh-checkout dependency audit also passed 301.
After activation, all 28 successor tests, Ruff and YAML parsing passed.
Automatic Source/Spark dependency traffic and synthetic forward/optimizer
counters are separate from the new native job; they were not measured here.

Local execution record:
`evidence/lumi-4b-sft-prepared-qualification-execution-v0.3.json`.
The record, this status and downloaded aggregates have not been pushed.

## Remaining boundary

Next, establish a bound plan for dedicated target-host/runtime and
external-writer admission, full-size resource admission and separately
authorized real S3 checkpoint CPU import. Then GPU worker/private-data/CUDA
smoke prerequisites, SFT, evaluation and deployment remain separate work.
This result does not authorize those actions or require turning on an H100 now.

No real pretrained checkpoint or dataset was accessed by this qualification.
GPU use, real import, target-host admission, source immutability, guardian-death
cleanup and job-teardown proof remain unclaimed. Training authorization and
production eligibility remain false. The old native failure evidence is
preserved; this successful successor does not prove its exact historical cause.
